                  <msItem>
                     <title>Fragm. operis incerti</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Binding fragment in a volume comprising two
                        incunabula: Domizio Calderini's commentary on Martial (Venice: Baptista de
                        Tortis, 1485) [ISTC im00308000] and Juvenal, with commentary of Antonio
                        Mancinello (Venice: Johannes Tacuinus, 1494/95) [ISTC ij00663000].
                        Contemporary Oxford binding, with Gibson, Early Oxford Bindings, stamp
                        B7.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The printed volume has 'Liber Rinandi Colyeri
                        Pretium [. . .]' on the blank recto of the dedication. Later owned by G.
                        Dunn; sold at Sotheby's, 2-6 Feb. 1914 (lot 1370) to Edwards (£3.7.0), and
                        bought by Alfred C. Chapin from Lathrop C. Harper, New York dealer, 29
                        November 1916.</note>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>Text concerns the rite of baptism.</title>
                     </msItem>
                  </msItem>
